      "math_academy_id": "q-182220",
      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "If $A=\\{a,b\\}$ and $B=\\{-1,0,1\\}$ then $|P(A)\\times P(B)|=$",
      "worked_solution": "For any set $S,$ we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ Also, $|S\\times T|=|S|\\cdot |T|.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n|A|=2,\\,|B|=3.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(A)| & ={2}^{|A|}={2}^{2}=4, \\\\ |P(B)| & ={2}^{|B|}={2}^{3}=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(A)\\times P(B)| & =|P(A)|\\cdot |P(B)| \\\\  & =4\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
